==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=huntress}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|hunteress}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|hunter|ess|lang=en}}, possibly on the model of the likes of {{m|en|mistress}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhʌntɹɪs/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|es}}

# A female [[hunter]].
#* '''1590''', {{w|Edmund Spenser}}, ''The Faerie Queene'', III.5:
#*: In those same woods ye well remember may / How that a noble '''hunteress''' did wonne [...].
#* '''2014''', William Kremer, ''[http://www.bbc.com/news/magazine-26969150 A 13-year-old eagle huntress in Mongolia]'', BBC World Service:
#*: Ashol-Pan, the daughter of a particularly celebrated hunter, may well be the country's only apprentice '''huntress'''.

